# ✅ **Q-4(b) — Differentiate: *const* member functions vs *static* member functions**

| Feature | const Member Function | static Member Function |
|--------|------------------------|-------------------------|
| Belongs to | Object | Class |
| Can modify object data? | ❌ No | ❌ Cannot access non-static data |
| Called using | Object only | Class name or object |
| Access to `this` pointer | ✔️ Yes | ❌ No |
| Example use | To ensure function doesn’t modify object | Common utility, count objects, shared data |

### **Example**

```cpp
class Demo {
    int x;
    static int count;

public:
    void show() const {   // const function
        // x++;  ❌ not allowed
        cout << x;
    }

    static void display() {  // static function
        cout << count;
    }
};
```

