# ✅ **METHOD 1 — Override names in derived class (BEST & SIMPLEST)**  
→ Make a **wrapper function** inside `NetSalary` to avoid scope resolution.

### ✔️ Updated Derived Class

```cpp
class NetSalary : public Gross, public Deduction {
public:
    void getAllData() {   // single function to get all inputs
        Gross::getdata();
        Deduction::getdata();
    }

    void showAllData() {  // single function to display everything
        Gross::displaydata();
        Deduction::displaydata();
    }

    void calculate() {
        float net = (basic + hra + da + ta) - (pf + tds);
        cout << "\nNet Salary = " << net << endl;
    }
};
```

### ✔️ And now main becomes super clean:

```cpp
int main() {
    NetSalary emp;

    emp.getAllData();

    cout << "\n--- Salary Details ---\n";
    emp.showAllData();

    emp.calculate();
}
```

👉 **No need for `emp.Gross::` or `emp.Deduction::`**

