# ✅ **METHOD 2 — Rename functions in parent classes**  
If both base classes have different names (no conflict), then calls are simple.

### Change function names:

```cpp
class Gross {
public:
    void getGrossData();
    void showGrossData();
};

class Deduction {
public:
    void getDeductionData();
    void showDeductionData();
};
```

### Main becomes:

```cpp
emp.getGrossData();
emp.getDeductionData();

emp.showGrossData();
emp.showDeductionData();
```

👉 No ambiguity → no scope resolution needed.

