# ✅ **METHOD 3 — Use `using` keyword inside derived class**

This avoids conflicts without wrapper functions.

```cpp
class NetSalary : public Gross, public Deduction {
public:
    using Gross::getdata;
    using Deduction::getdata;

    using Gross::displaydata;
    using Deduction::displaydata;
};
```

### Now main:

```cpp
emp.Gross::getdata();       // still possible
emp.Deduction::getdata();   // still possible

emp.displaydata();  // now allowed (but ambiguous if you don't specify)
```

👉 This method is less clean — but valid.

